    {
      "id": "make",
      "name": "Make",
      "category": "ShapeInstance",
      "signature": "Make(In Shape Idx, In Geometry)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "In Shape Idx",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Geometry",
          "type": "TSerializablePtr<FImplicitObject>"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniquePtr<FShapeInstanceProxy>",
      "docs": "NOTE: FShapeInstanceProxy is a Game-Thread object.\nSee FShapeInstance for the physics-thread equivalent\nFShapeInstanceProxy contains the per-shape data associated with a single shape on a particle.\nThis contains data like the collision / query filters, material properties etc.\nEvery particle holds one FShapeInstanceProxy object for each geometry they use.\nIf the particle has a Union of geometries there will be one FShapeInstanceProxy\nfor each geometry in the union. (Except ClusteredUnions - these are not flattened\nbecause they contain their own query acceleration structure.)\nNOTE: keep size to a minimum. There can be millions of these in s scene.\n@todo(chaos) : try to remove the GT Proxy pointer - this could easily be passed into the\nrelevant functions instead.\n@todo(chaos) : reduce the cost of MaterialData for shapes with one materialand no masks etc."
    },
